                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9cadcf64-a4c6-4adc-a3f3-ea1c1085fd29",
                        "source_entry_id": "7d17f744-8eaa-39a4-b9a1-a43c15b38ff0",
                        "source_sense_id": "53908d55-3b13-3598-b662-de0bc62200ad",
                        "source_sense_description": "op geel lijkend",
                        "target_lang_word": "yellowish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "yellowish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4b90301-036d-31a8-886d-2b6b8a569ec9",
                                        "entry_id": "e1807fbc-8954-3d62-b73c-cacb50ef0699",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somewhat yellow in colour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a72b4a0-f024-4c49-8deb-aee02c4a5590",
                                                "sense_id": "d4b90301-036d-31a8-886d-2b6b8a569ec9",
                                                "text": "But, like more than one similar North Wales beauty-spot, there had to be (at least at the time of which I write), a quarry, or ironworks, or some kind of industrial plant, which lay perpetually under a cloud of yellowish smoke—literally a blot on the landscape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0294f411-c15f-4d99-a8d0-0a6b0c038084",
                                                "sense_id": "d4b90301-036d-31a8-886d-2b6b8a569ec9",
                                                "text": "A biologist has named a newly discovered species of moth after our next president. The Neopalpa donaldtrumpi is a wee little creature found in parts of California and Baja, Mexico. […] It seems nature favors fancy golden hairdos as much as the man himself (who could forget China’s beloved Trump bird?), because the N. donaldtrumpi sports a very familiar-looking crown of yellowish scales."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed58b736-ea63-4806-9427-3782dc297d54",
                        "source_entry_id": "7d17f744-8eaa-39a4-b9a1-a43c15b38ff0",
                        "source_sense_id": "53908d55-3b13-3598-b662-de0bc62200ad",
                        "source_sense_description": "op geel lijkend",
                        "target_lang_word": "jaunâtre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jaunâtre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "726087d6-6821-359b-93eb-537ead874c45",
                                        "entry_id": "9dd88045-f05e-376a-afb9-8379076d8916",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui tire sur le jaune."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24be34cc-bad0-4a07-84fd-192ef0d4955c",
                                                "sense_id": "726087d6-6821-359b-93eb-537ead874c45",
                                                "text": "Mais tous ses soins furent pour le salon. Elle réussit presque à en faire un lieu habitable. Il était garni d’un meuble de velours jaunâtre, à fleurs satinées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "993eafbe-5bb5-40ee-b6a6-8ec35c256c74",
                                                "sense_id": "726087d6-6821-359b-93eb-537ead874c45",
                                                "text": "Une pâte de corozo, préparée d’après une recette qu’il avait inventée, lui permettait également de fabriquer des dés d’une nuance jaunâtre, comme si l’on s’en était longtemps servi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec94c34e-5d6b-4231-8ddc-8acba5438278",
                                                "sense_id": "726087d6-6821-359b-93eb-537ead874c45",
                                                "text": "Mais la terre jaunâtre et glaiseuse du Perche, désignée dans le pays sous le nom de gruette ou de bournais, exige périodiquement des marnages, en raison de son acidité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
